                <li>☐ Optimize rewards based on profitable behavior.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="faq">
            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <h3>What is referral revenue attribution?</h3>

            <p>
                Referral revenue attribution is the process of connecting revenue to a specific referral source according to defined tracking and attribution rules.
            </p>

            <h3>Why is referral ROI important?</h3>

            <p>
                Referral ROI helps determine whether the revenue generated by the referral program justifies its financial and operational costs.
            </p>

            <h3>Should points be counted as revenue?</h3>

            <p>
                Points themselves should not automatically be treated as revenue. Track points separately and analyze how they influence purchases, referrals, and customer engagement.
            </p>

            <h3>Should repeat purchases be included?</h3>

            <p>
                They can be included when your attribution rules support them. The important thing is to define the rule consistently and avoid overstating referral revenue.
            </p>

            <h3>How often should referral ROI be measured?</h3>

            <p>
                Monthly measurement is a practical starting point for many programs. High-volume programs may benefit from more frequent monitoring.
            </p>

            <h3>How can email marketing improve referral ROI?</h3>

            <p>
                Email can increase referral participation, remind customers about points, encourage additional referrals, support repeat purchases, and strengthen customer retention.
            </p>
